<title>SWITZERLAND: CYCLING-TOUR OF SWITZERLAND THIRD STAGE PLACINGS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-TOUR OF SWITZERLAND THIRD STAGE PLACINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LA CHAUX DE FONDS, Switzerland 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading</p>
<p>placings in the 202-km third stage of the Tour of Switzerland</p>
<p>from Basle to La Chaux de Fonds on Thursday:</p>
<p>1. Christophe Agnolutto (France) 4 hours 30 minutes 23 seconds</p>
<p>2. Max Van Heeswijk (Netherlands)  2 minutes 34 seconds behind</p>
<p> 3. Valentino Fois (Italy)		same time</p>
<p> 4. Marco Vergnani (Italy)		6:52</p>
<p> 5. Rof Aldag (Germany)		  11:32</p>
<p>6. Gilles Bouvard (France)</p>
<p>7. Mauro Bettin (Italy)</p>
<p>8. Lauri Aus (Estonia)</p>
<p>9. Fabio Baldato (Italy)</p>
<p>10. Aart Vierhouten (Netherlands)</p>
<p>11. Niki Aebersold (Switzerland)</p>
<p>12. Udo Boelts (Germany)</p>
<p>13. Luca Mazanti (Italy)</p>
<p>14. Jon Odriozola (Spain)</p>
<p> 15. Cristiano Colleoni (Italy)	all same time</p>
<p>Leading overall placings after three stages:</p>
<p> 1. Agnolutto	   9 hours 33 minutes 7 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Van Heeswijk			    2:34 behind</p>
<p> 3. Fois					2:55</p>
<p> 4. Vergnani				  9:04</p>
<p> 5. Oskar Camenzind (Switzerland)    11:23</p>
<p> 6. Leon Van Bon (Netherlands)	 same time</p>
<p> 7. Roberto Petito (Italy)	     11:28</p>
<p> 8. Danny Nelissen (Belgium)	   11:30</p>
<p> 9. Boelts				   11:37</p>
<p> 10. Juergen Werner Germany)	   11:42</p>
